  "requestTimestamp": "2026-07-19T01:13:46.619Z",
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nAn individual with ₱250,000 gross compensation income in 2024 is not required to file an income tax return, as this amount falls within the tax-exempt threshold.\n\n### Controlling Authorities\nThis is governed by Section 24 of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC), which states that individuals with a taxable income not exceeding ₱250,000 are exempt from income tax.\n\n### Interpretation\nAccording to the tax schedule effective from January 1, 2023, individuals earning not over ₱250,000 are subject to a 0% tax rate. Furthermore, Section 51-A of the NIRC provides that employees receiving purely compensation income from a single employer, where the tax has been correctly withheld, are not required to file an annual income tax return.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nFor the individual in question, since their gross compensation income is exactly ₱250,000, they are not liable for income tax and thus do not need to file a return. This simplifies their tax obligations and reduces administrative burdens, as their employer's withholding tax certificate suffices for compliance.",
